It builds on, and runs, the following work under their own terms.

Engine
- vLLM (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm), Apache-2.0. The image is
  upstream vLLM's wheel for commit a0d7356b98, the fork's vLLM branch over it and
  the vllm-cmp170hx plugin, all from https://github.com/AlexBrandes/vllm, also
  Apache-2.0 (see that repository's NOTICE), on NVIDIA's CUDA 13.0 Ubuntu 24.04
  base image.
- The plugin's layout, startup guard and seam tooling are adapted from
  vllm-sm80 by Morrowmake (https://github.com/Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx),
  Apache-2.0.
- The engine's Qwen3.8-27B support ports several changes from HyperQwen by
  syv-ai (https://github.com/syv-ai/HyperQwen), Apache-2.0: the int8 embedding
  and LM-head loading, the MTP draft vocabulary, the int8-activation Marlin
  changes and the split-KV speculative-decode attention kernel.
- The K3 Marlin route dispatcher is generated from vLLM's Marlin host code
  (Apache-2.0); the INT8 GEMMs use NVIDIA CUTLASS (BSD-3-Clause) headers as
  shipped in the vLLM wheel.

Model
- Qwen3.8-27B by the Qwen team, Apache-2.0. The W4A16 checkpoint
  dbirks/Qwen3.8-27B-W4A16-AutoRound was made with intel/auto-round
  (Apache-2.0); syvai/qwen3.8-27b-3090-fast-variant (int4 LM head, MTP module,
  draft vocabulary) is Apache-2.0.
- The DFlash2 drafter syvai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-W4A16 is a W4A16 requantization
  of incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2; both Apache-2.0.
- This repository ships no weights: download.sh fetches them from their model
  pages.

Benchmarks
- Speed tables use the sparkDash protocol (MiaAI-Lab/sparkDash, commit
  3e6d4ef, Apache-2.0); its prompts are used as data with attribution.
- GSM8K (OpenAI, MIT) as distributed with vLLM's tests/evals/gsm8k, HumanEval
  (OpenAI, MIT), and GPQA Diamond (Rein et al., CC BY 4.0) with the prompt and
  answer pattern of OpenAI simple-evals (MIT).

